three.js 0.186.1 (npm 'three'). MIT license: three.LICENSE
One local patch (2026-10-11), to re-apply on an update: build/three.module.js
WebGLState.setPolygonOffset negates `units` as well as `factor` with a reversed depth
buffer. Unpatched, a negative units (meant to pull a surface toward the camera) pushed it
away; with a fixed-point depth buffer, the belly camera's 5 cm near plane and a narrow
zoom, the drawn roads fell behind the ground (the owner's screenshot).
- build/three.module.js, build/three.core.js
- addons/objects/Sky.js (examples/jsm/objects/Sky.js), imported as three/addons/objects/Sky.js

Barlow Condensed (Google Fonts v13, weights 400/500/600, latin subset), unmodified.
SIL Open Font License 1.1: fonts/OFL.txt. fonts/barlow-condensed.css holds the
@font-face rules from Google Fonts with local file names.
